    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "where $ c_s = k_1/k_2 $, $ c_e = (k_2 - k_1)/k_2 $, and $ Q = c_s \\text{MS}_s + c_e \\text{MS}_e $. This estimate of $ r $ is really only a first-order approximation, as Satterthwaite’s derivation assumes that the observed mean squares in the function Q are independently distributed, a condition that is not strictly true with an unbalanced design.",
