      "content_sha256": "762354adff2010a75d7645331acdc67f9b72bae3cfcfb8342e908c26d6d68a33"
    },
    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "where $ c_s = k_1/(k_2 + k_3) $ and $ c_e = (k_2 + k_3 - k_1)/(k_2 + k_3) $. The numerator degrees of freedom is approximated by Equation 18.35c, with $ Q = c_sMS_s + c_eMS_e $.",
      "source_page": 590,
      "printed_page": 570,
      "source_block_ids": [
        "Genetics_chapter18:p024:b6"
      ],
      "bbox": [
        135.0,
